1067 0 obj
<</Title(1-Matplotlib and Seaborn -The Matplotlib and Seaborn libraries are used to create visual representations of the data, including scatter plots, bar charts, and line graphs. These visualizations help reveal patterns and relationships between different variables, such as: -How flight number varies across launch sites -The connection between payload mass and launch site -the relationship between orbit type and the success rate 2-Folium  -The Folium library is applied to build interactive maps for geographic analysis. It is used to: -Display all launch sites on a map -Highlight successful and failed launches at each location -Show distances between launch sites and nearby points of interest, such as cities, railways, and highways 3-Dash The Dash framework is used to build an interactive web application that allows users to explore the data through controls such as dropdown menus and range sliders. With the help of visualizations like pie charts and scatter plots, the app enables users to: -View the total number of successful launches for each launch site -Examine the relationship between payload mass and mission outcome \(success or failure\) across different launch sites)/Dest[17 0 R/Fit]/Parent 1061 0 R>>
endobj

